WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.040
Just being at your side,

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:16.160
Gentles my hearts to the point of disbelief

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:25.570
I thought I heard the sound of your footsteps behind me,

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:35.720
I turned my head repeatedly, wishing you would appear...

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:41.740
...and then there you were

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:50.990
The beginning of a new love

00:00:51.310 --> 00:01:05.870
Is unknowingly, the beginning of our invisible love story

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:15.360
Hence, I shall never leave your side

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:24.540
I pledge to love you and only you

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:48.730
<i>You switched shampoos.</i>

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:49.440
<i>Can you tell?</i>

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:03.250
<i>One by one, my classmates</i> <i>have been disappearing.</i>

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.530
<i>Atsushi joined the army,</i>

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.020
<i>Take was killed in the</i> <i>Sapporo air raid,</i>

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.990
<i>and his girlfriend, Yukari,</i> <i>just stopped coming.</i>

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:21.900
<i>But I'm still here,</i> <i>unable to see any reason</i>

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:23.470
<i>to move forward.</i>

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:32.070
CULTURE FESTIVAL EXECUTIVE COMMITTEE<b>
THE CULTURE FESTIVAL!!
BRING BACK</b>

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.120
Can you still love a girl like me?

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.090
Shuji!

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:44.960
Akemi.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.820
Uh, bye-bye!

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:49.790
Yeah...

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:02.410
<i>I was getting used to</i> <i>Chise not being around.</i>

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.020
<i>Little by little, I was starting</i> <i>to like this town.</i>

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:10.220
Wait!

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.880
Come on!

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:14.490
Ouch!

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.990
She's always crying.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:20.290
You OK?

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:21.560
Come now...

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.260
Let's go.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:33.310
<i>It was loss that</i> <i>started me remembering</i>

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:37.740
<i>all these things about this town</i> <i>I'd spent my life in.</i>

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:45.480
"Everyone's Changing"

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.530
Hey Hana, going on patrol?

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.010
Hana's nice and all, but...

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:13.480
I wish I could've spent more time with Akemi.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:18.080
I wonder what she's doing now... and Shuji too.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:22.860
Sis...

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:23.920
What?

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.260
What are you going to do about Shuji...

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:30.500
Satomi, I have a boyfriend now.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:34.370
He told me he loves me.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:38.040
See? I can do it too.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.340
Sis...

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.590
That's good!

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:02.890
Sounds like drums.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.990
Drums?

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:08.000
The marching band's practicing hard.

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:09.400
Those losers!

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.180
<i>So this is what war's like.</i>

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:18.610
<i>And I thought I'd be here,</i>

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:21.750
<i>fighting to protect Akemi...</i>

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:25.850
Oh, it's meat!

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:31.130
This is the best part of being in the army, huh?

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:35.560
Yeah. Too bad for the folks back home starving, though.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:37.190
Huh?

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:40.460
Hana's still on patrol?

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:44.200
She's dead.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:49.710
There was a skirmish with enemy scouts in the Western sector.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:57.260
So those weren't drums we heard...

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:03.330
Her boyfriend died of injuries after the Sapporo raid, so she enlisted.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:08.460
Too bad she couldn't have taken at least one of them with her.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:26.550
Hey, Shuji!

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:28.350
Did you hear?

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:29.280
What?

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:34.020
There's a downed enemy pilot hiding in the hills.

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:38.060
The local militia's going after him.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:41.860
Yukari's going too. Want to come?

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:44.860
No thanks...

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:47.600
No?

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:49.300
Well, see ya.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:50.240
Yeah.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:18.360
Fall asleep and you're dead.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:19.900
Lieutenant Tetsu!

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:22.640
Quiet, dummy.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:26.810
Someone came this way just now.

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:30.410
I'm sorry, sir. I didn't see anyone!

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:36.520
That's because, in your head, you're still at peace.

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:40.970
That's nice. You can die happy and peaceful.

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:42.720
I - I...

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:46.030
Be quiet. You won't get home alive, anyway.

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:48.860
I'm going out there.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:52.290
Whatever happens, don't back me up, got it?

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:54.360
Wha...?

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:58.910
I don't want some fool shooting me in the back by mistake.

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:03.050
Civilian refugee? Enemy scout?

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.040
Civilians are such a pain...

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:06.950
Huh?

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.680
Enemies you can just kill...

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:29.570
Crying again?

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:32.740
It's been awhile...

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:34.940
Tetsu...

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:01.270
A dream...?

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.520
So, you're awake?

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:10.740
Tetsu! Um... where are we?

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:13.310
My hideout.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.280
If you're awake, let's get some food.

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:19.820
You mean, at the base?

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.080
Don't worry, just follow me.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:24.230
Uh, OK!

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:33.670
Another fine day...

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:36.530
What is it?

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:38.770
Tetsu, keep it down.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.340
It's OK.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:43.140
But we're near the enemy camp now.

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:46.880
Don't worry. Besides, I'm with you.

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:47.880
Me?

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:54.860
That's fine, but if I activate, you'll die.

00:09:57.060 --> 00:10:00.330
That happens all the time now.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.460
Things we need, things we don't, all just blown away.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:12.510
I don't even realize it, and suddenly everyone's gone.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:17.010
Don't do that!

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:20.610
It's OK. Nobody'll notice two or three shots.

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:24.980
That's not it! I mean, I might go off!

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:27.790
You'll die! I mean it!

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:31.160
Then how are we gonna get breakfast?!

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:34.230
All right, I'll open it!

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:49.540
Good, huh, Chise?

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:53.010
So, how's your boyfriend?

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:56.480
What was it, Shoji, or Yuji something?

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:00.420
We're just classmates now.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:06.090
Well, now that we've eaten, let's go shopping.

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.890
There's no point saving money anymore.

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:12.580
I thought I'd spend it while I can.

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:16.470
Don't worry about it.

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:19.930
No one will complain if Commander Chise

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:23.940
goes back to being an ordinary girl for a day.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:26.640
Tetsu...

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:43.600
What is it, sir?

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:47.710
It's an emergency. I need to requisition your bike.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:49.710
An emergency?

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:52.770
I'm not at liberty to disclose the details.

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:55.150
I need to transport someone.

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:57.440
It's Commander Chise.

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:01.420
Y - Yes sir!

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:04.880
But I need to report in regularly.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:08.690
So if I could clear this with Headquarters...

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:11.390
Your name and unit?

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:15.660
Sergeant Kimura, Headquarters Signal Unit.

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:17.730
Hmm, I'll remember that.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:22.700
By the way, I'm in a big hurry.

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:30.410
What have I just done?

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:37.420
They still haven't found him...

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:42.550
I'd rather be killed than captured.

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:46.390
What if it were Atsushi out there?!

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:49.460
Do you think he'd be better off dead?!

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:53.070
How can you talk about death so lightly?

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.670
How can you say that when people are dying?!

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:17.420
Leaving early again?

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:18.350
Yeah.

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:22.280
I was about to leave too.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:27.100
It's so cold in there, and it's all study periods now anyway.

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:27.830
Yeah.

00:13:35.650 --> 00:13:37.880
Atsushi's a fool.

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:42.710
Who would go to war just for a girl like me?

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:44.250
That idiot.

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:50.420
It bothers me a lot.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:55.690
What am I supposed to do? I hate to say this, but...

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:58.960
Atsushi scared me...

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:04.010
Idiot!

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:06.330
Don't talk about Atsushi like that!

00:14:07.520 --> 00:14:11.240
I hate myself for feeling this way!

00:14:14.390 --> 00:14:17.860
But I understand. I'm scared too!

00:14:19.990 --> 00:14:22.050
Should he be killing people for me?

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:23.590
Is that really OK?

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:25.150
Is it right?!

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:29.500
How can I live with myself now?!

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:30.890
Shuji!

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:35.710
What if he kills someone for my sake?

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:38.490
Sure it sucks, dummy!

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:42.640
But Atsushi told me, right or wrong,

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:46.150
he wanted to protect you.

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:50.480
He might kill someone, and he might get killed.

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:54.160
But who can say that's wrong?!

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:59.490
And who can claim that they're right in all this?

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:01.060
Shuji...

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:03.860
It's the same with Chise and me.

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:06.930
Words like "girlfriend," "classmate,"

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:09.540
they mean nothing, really.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.240
Which is right, or wrong...

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:14.840
it's not about that.

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:18.480
I've been struggling...

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:20.580
for weeks with this.

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:27.460
We're OK. You, me, Atsushi, Chise, Nori too,

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:32.220
maybe Yukari too, I'm not sure,

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:38.400
but if we're struggling, then it means we're alive!

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:41.280
You bastard...!

00:15:55.250 --> 00:15:56.550
Take!!!

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:13.390
We'll all be OK.

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:19.410
Shuji...

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:22.680
Let's go. We don't want to catch cold.

00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:26.680
There's no more medicine, so if you get sick, it's all over.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:34.050
I bet Atsushi's getting well fed where he is.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:42.460
Sure he is. He's a soldier, after all.

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:44.990
He always did eat a lot.

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:48.240
Lucky guy. I'm always hungry.

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:52.740
Mmm, me too. I'd love a good meal.

00:16:54.850 --> 00:16:55.610
Yeah.

00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:57.850
Akemi...

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:05.690
I'm hungry, that's all.

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:09.950
Dummy.

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:26.540
Have you found Chise yet?

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:32.080
She requisitioned a Signal Corps motorcycle at 1030 hours today,

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:34.180
and hasn't been seen since.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:36.880
What a nuisance she is.

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:39.980
She certainly is.

00:17:40.590 --> 00:17:43.620
Well, negotiations with the enemy are proceeding.

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:46.050
Let's hope we can get out of this peacefully.

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:47.700
Let's hope...

00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:53.500
Man, it sure takes a woman forever to buy clothes.

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:56.000
Sorry, this is the last one.

00:17:57.310 --> 00:18:01.970
<i>Fuyumi, I'm sorry. I'm on a date</i> <i>with a young girl now.</i>

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:07.110
<i>She was lonely and depressed,</i> <i>she reminded me of you.</i>

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:12.810
A spy plane?

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:17.760
No!

00:18:19.230 --> 00:18:20.310
Chise!

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:23.150
Stop it, please!

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:24.830
No!

00:18:29.970 --> 00:18:32.410
Stop! Help!

00:18:32.990 --> 00:18:34.540
Chise, I'm coming!

00:18:37.810 --> 00:18:38.520
Tetsu!

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:40.180
I can't stop...!

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:41.950
What the...?!

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:46.690
Help me...

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:49.010
Chise, hold on!

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:52.490
It's all right! The enemy's gone!

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:53.390
Chise!

00:18:56.430 --> 00:18:57.510
Tetsu...

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:13.570
Chise, sorry about that.

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:18.310
I'm OK. It's you who must have been repulsed by that,

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:21.120
kissing a girl with a body like mine.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.060
That's not true.

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:31.570
I'm tired. I can't go on.

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:34.610
Quiet, will you? We're out of gas, I told you.

00:19:34.970 --> 00:19:37.600
It's only ten kilometers, so stop whining.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:40.810
I don't like your attitude!

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:45.270
I outrank you, you know.

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:49.050
Then feel free to fly home, "Commander."

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:54.390
Go on home.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:57.850
We'll do it again, OK Chise?

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:01.420
No, we won't.

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:02.470
Chise...

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:06.060
No more promises.

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:10.960
I can't explain it, but I'm a weapon now,

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:13.000
and I can tell.

00:20:13.910 --> 00:20:18.080
At most, this town has three days of peace left.

00:20:18.220 --> 00:20:21.810
A little over two days and ten hours, to be precise.

00:20:21.890 --> 00:20:25.970
Headquarters is trying to negotiate, but it's too late.

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:29.820
The other side's got no choice but to advance.

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:34.500
More than half of them have nowhere to go back to.

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:39.000
And I've wiped out their supply lines and escape routes.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:43.530
Our army's strength is down to 24 per cent.

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:48.040
Air Force: 0.02 per cent. Navy: 1.2 per cent.

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:51.470
And the population is down to-

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:52.990
Chise! That's enough!

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:57.810
The peace in this town won't last much longer.

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:02.420
I'm giving you an order.

00:21:03.190 --> 00:21:03.920
Yes, ma'am.

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:08.620
I don't want to go home yet...

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:12.600
Thank you. Shuji, today,

00:21:12.970 --> 00:21:16.070
you were kind of cool. I mean it.

00:21:17.390 --> 00:21:18.710
I feel better.

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:20.140
Yeah.

00:21:20.650 --> 00:21:21.740
See ya, Shuji!

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:28.640
<i>This town, its people,</i> <i>the whole planet, is changing.</i>

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:32.120
<i>My family and friends</i> <i>will change too.</i>

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:38.920
<i>And so will Chise.</i> <i>There's no stopping it.</i>

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:02.020
Is this OK?

00:22:04.390 --> 00:22:08.420
You're going to die soon, anyway.

00:22:22.640 --> 00:22:26.970
<i>That night, a big earthquake</i> <i>struck our town.</i>

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:43.420
A rift opened up upon my heart

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:49.990
And I went through the night sleepless, sighing constantly

00:22:50.670 --> 00:22:59.340
Before I realize, it's turned to morning

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:08.660
I want to hear your voice

00:23:09.180 --> 00:23:13.250
I want to feel your warmth

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:19.460
Thoughts of you well up within me

00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:25.310
And my tears begin to overflow

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:36.570
Goodbye my beloved, I am still unable to forget about you

00:23:36.730 --> 00:23:46.740
Having all of this end with just a single word of goodbye

00:23:47.240 --> 00:23:51.570
Fills me with sorrow

00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:04.570
Chise! Our town, the park, the swings... it's all been...

00:24:04.810 --> 00:24:09.250
And our friend since we were little, she's been...

00:24:09.550 --> 00:24:10.280
Dammit!

00:24:10.750 --> 00:24:14.240
SAIKANO, Episode 9: "Akemi"
